battlefield fives war stories focused on  more of the unexplored and unknown parts  of world war two taking inspirations  from lesser-known conflicts and bringing  these stories and exploits to life  through the vignette of a single  individual the value of these stories is  how they present a much more personal  conflict there's no storming the beaches  of Normandy or assault on Stalingrad and  I think this is why the war stories both  in battlefield 1 and battlefield 5  really struck a chord with me  they were impactful in a way that I  didn't expect and told a story that most  modern media hadn't touched upon with  the release of the last tiger I was  thinking about other stories that would  fit the intimate war story formula and  remembered the battle for Castle it's  the only time in the Second World War  where Germany and America allied and  what historical accounts referred to as  the strangest battle of World War two  now I know EA have said that they have  no more plans or war stories in the  future but that shouldn't stop us from  talking about what moments in history  could make impactful transitions into  video games the battle was one of the  final events in the European theater  taking place five days after Hitler's  suicide and only two days before the  unconditional surrender of Germany  although most interestingly it is the  only time in the Second World War where  the forces of the Allies and German  powers would fight alongside each other  Castle itza was claimed as a prison camp  in 1943 with its purpose to house  high-profile French prisoners that were  valuable to the Reich occupants included  renowned tennis player Jean Barra former  Prime Minister's Edouard Daladier and  Paul Renard as well as a number of other  influential French individuals and  Eastern European prisoners that worked  around and maintained the castle after  the SS commander and troops are banned  in the castle the French prisoners took  up arms and attempted to summon aid from  the nearby town of org knowing that if  the SS troops were to return to the  castle they would be executed a  messenger was able to contact Austrian  resistance the head of which was a major  yosef dangle a Verma officer who was  against the Nazi regime and had defied  orders to retreat and instead join the  resistance major gang all travelled to  the nearby town of kufstein where he  surrendered to a US Armored Division led  by a captain John see Jack Lee jr.  presenting the situation to the captain  he pled for aid and a rescue attempt to  free the French prisoners Lee  volunteered to lead the rescue mission  without hesitation immediately earning  permission from the US HQ although  through the common  of rough terrain an unstable bridge men  that Lee would have to leave the bulk of  his armor and reinforcements behind and  in the end he was forced to head to the  castle with only his Sherman tank 14  American soldiers major Kangol his  driver and a truck carrying 10 German  artillery man as the combined forces of  the Americans and the ver market arrived  the prisoners now led by an SS officer  they had befriended while he was  recovering from wounds offered a warm  welcome but were rather disappointed in  the small size of the group that had  come to save them knowing that an  attacking force could arrive at any  moment the next morning of forced  numbering between 150 to 200 waffen-ss  opened fire on the castle from the tree  lines with them they bought a flak 88  anti-tank gun which damaged both the  castle and destroyed the Sherman tank  that was providing machine-gun fire as  the day went on the Allied group was  suffering injuries and casualties even  suffering the loss of major Ganga  himself who was killed by a rifle round  while he was attempting to get former  prime minister Reynard to safety as  there was no line of communication for  the castle reinforcements were unaware  of enemy disposition knowing that the  key to victory lay in ensuring those  reinforcements were able to get to the  castle quickly and with up-to-date  information tennis star Bharata offered  to run through the attacking SS dodging  strong points and ambushes to deliver  up-to-date information  miraculously managing to survive and  reach the American reinforcements he  requested a uniform a weapon and  ammunition joining the force as they  made haste to the castle to relieve the  defenders as the occupants the castle  were nearly out of ammunition and  prepared for the enemy force to breach  the walls help finally arrived and a  4:00 p.m. the SS were quickly defeated  by the tanks and infantry of the relief  force resulting in approximately 100 SS  soldiers being taken prisoner only two  days later Germany would formally sign  their unconditional surrender  for his heroic deeds Lee would receive  the Distinguished Service Cross and for  giving his life in the battle Ganga was  honored as an Austrian national hero  even having a street in the nearby Vogel  named in his honor  similar to the current suite of war  stories are recounting this battle  aligns perfectly with the intimacy that  this series already presents and it's a  chance to shed light on another seldom  told story with the same intimacy that  is already present in the series as well  as it being a chance for interesting  characters and intense set pieces  imagine it being told from a multitude  of perspectives  the French prisoner who is unsure of  their future being locked away from the  world the ver mark soldier whose country  is about to lose the war and has to seek  help from the Army they were fighting  against only a few weeks prior the  American soldier having to put aside any  hatred for the enemy for the greater  good and for the safety of the  imprisoned imagine all these individuals  some with extremely polarizing views  experiences and opinions and not only  the war but of each other being thrust  together in an attempt to survive all  under overwhelming odds gameplay why is  a castle it's a war story could include  sections where prisoners are delivering  messages and reinforcements they would  allow stealth and guile and the main  battle could not only provide the  spectacle of a classic battlefield  set-piece with the lack of ammunition  and manpower also playing directly into  battlefield fives attrition system but  players would also be forced to make  every shot count from the position of  the castle walls waiting for  reinforcements to appear on the horizon  I think it's also important to bring  people's attention to the battle itself  as I said before it's about humanity  putting aside their differences for  getting past conflicts and working  together so that they may help those in  need after listening to the recounting  of one of the strangest battles of World  War two I think you can understand why  it would be perfect to be featured as a  war story in battlefield 5 not only is  it a bizarre story but also offers the  opportunity for a deeply personal look  at a part of the second world war with  close-knit groups of people being thrust  together in utterly uncompromising  circumstances considering how unique the  event is it's surprising to see that it  is mostly gone unexplored by modern  media sure of an awesome track off of  sabatons 2016 album The Last Stand if  you found this snippet interesting  though I could only go into so much  detail with the battle so I really  recommend you go read up about it  yourself as it is a fascinating part of  the Second World War but to any other  history enthusiasts with tales to share  I want to know what you think would make  an awesome battlefield war story one  explored events would you'd like to see  explored on the small screen let me know  in the comment section below or find me  on twitter at a regular Dave for now  thanks for watching and I will see you  in the next one
 

